# Refee Web — environment
#
# These MUST point at the same Supabase project as the mobile app. One project
# = one set of user accounts, so a referee who signs up on the web can sign in
# on the app and vice versa.

# ── Local development (matches the app's `npm run start:local`) ──────────────
#
# The seeded test accounts — (555) 555-0100 … 0105, OTP always 123456 — live in
# the LOCAL Supabase stack, not in any hosted project. To use them here:
#
#   1. cd ../Refee-Mobile/refee && supabase start
#   2. cd back here and run: npm run setup:local
#      (reads `supabase status` and writes .env.local for you)
#   3. npm run dev       → open http://localhost:3000/auth/sign-in
#
# To fill this in by hand instead, copy the API URL and the Publishable key
# from `supabase status` — NOT the sb_secret_… / service-role key.
#
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_...paste-from-supabase-status...

# ── Hosted (staging / production) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase → Project Settings → API. Must match the app's EXPO_PUBLIC_* values.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Stripe — same publishable key as the app's EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY.
# Used by Stripe Elements for "pay crew" and saving a card for auto-pay.
# Optional locally: leave unset and the payment sheets show a setup notice.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxx

# development | staging | production
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=development
